sections.body_md:
**Partnership** (Section 4): the relation between persons who have agreed to share the profits of a business carried on by all of them or by any of them acting for all.

**Features:** two or more persons (at most 50, under the Companies Act, 2013 and its rules); an agreement, oral or written; a lawful business; sharing of profits; mutual agency; unlimited liability. Registration is optional, but an unregistered firm cannot sue outsiders to enforce a contract.

**Provisions on accounts and rights** (unless partners agree otherwise):
- partners must be just and faithful to each other and render true accounts and full information (Section 9);
- every partner may take part in the conduct of the business (Section 12);
- ordinary matters are decided by majority; the nature of the business changes only with the consent of all (Section 12);
- every partner may have access to, inspect and copy any of the books of the firm (Section 12).

**Partnership deed:** the written agreement among partners, signed and stamped. It usually covers names and business, duration, capitals (fixed or fluctuating), profit-sharing ratio, interest on capital, drawings, current balances and loans, salaries and commission, any guarantee of profit, accounting rules, and rules for admission, retirement, death, goodwill, disputes and dissolution.

**When the deed is silent (Section 13):**
- profits and losses shared **equally**;
- **no** salary or commission to any partner;
- **no** interest on capital; where interest is agreed, it is payable **only out of profits**;
- **no** interest on drawings;
- interest on a partner's **loan or advance** at **6% per annum**, a charge against profit, from the date of the advance.

**Format:** credit net profit (after all charges), interest on drawings and interest on debit current balances; debit interest on capital and on credit current balances, partners' salary and commission, transfer to reserve; the balance (**divisible profit**) is credited to partners in the profit-sharing ratio.

**Interest on capital:** on opening capital for the year; on additions from their date; reduced for withdrawals from their date.
- deed silent: none;
- appropriation, enough profit: full interest;
- appropriation, profit short: the whole profit shared in the **ratio of interest due**;
- appropriation, loss: none (Section 13: payable only out of profits);
- charge: full interest debited to the Profit and Loss Account, even if it causes a loss.

**Commission:**
- a **manager's** commission is a charge (Profit and Loss or Profit and Loss Adjustment Account);
- a **partner's** commission is an appropriation;
- on profit before charging it: profit × rate ÷ 100; after charging it: profit × rate ÷ (100 + rate).

A partner is promised a minimum share of profit. Divide the profit (after interest, salary and other appropriations, unless the guarantee says otherwise) in the normal ratio; if the share is below the minimum, the **deficiency** is borne by:
- the **firm**: the other partners in their mutual profit-sharing ratio;
- **one partner**: that partner alone;
- **two or more partners**: in the ratio they agreed (their profit ratio if none is stated).

Show the guarantors' reduced shares and the guaranteed partner's minimum in the appropriation account, or pass an entry: guarantor's capital (or current) A/c Dr., to guaranteed partner's capital (or current) A/c.

In a **loss** year the guarantee still holds: deficiency = minimum + the guaranteed partner's share of loss. The firm's total profit or loss never changes.
